IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 3: SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION, ss 19 to 26A.
-- Policy for "unless the contrary intention appears": a plain yes/no input, NOTHING when it is TRUE.

§ `Section 19 -- general provisions with respect to the power to make subsidiary legislation`

-- src:1141 | 19. When any Act confers powers on any authority to make
-- src:1142 | subsidiary legislation, the following provisions have effect with
-- src:1143 | reference to the making and operation of the subsidiary legislation
-- src:1144 | unless the contrary intention appears:
-- src:1146 | (a) subsidiary legislation may at any time be amended, varied,
-- src:1147 | rescinded or revoked by the same authority and in the same
-- src:1148 | manner by and in which it was made subject to the
-- src:1149 | following provisions:
@ref s 19(a) (src:1141-1149)
GIVEN `the power is exercised by the same authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the same manner in which the subsidiary legislation was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsidiary legislation may be amended, varied, rescinded or revoked at any time` `the power is exercised by the same authority` `in the same manner in which the subsidiary legislation was made` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) AND `the power is exercised by the same authority` AND `in the same manner in which the subsidiary legislation was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1151 | (i) where any Act is to come into operation on a date to
-- src:1152 | be fixed by subsidiary legislation, the power to make
-- src:1153 | the subsidiary legislation does not include the power
-- src:1154 | of amending, revoking or suspending the same; and
@ref s 19(a)(i) (src:1151-1154)
GIVEN `an Act is to come into operation on a date to be fixed by subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to fix the date includes the power to amend, revoke or suspend the subsidiary legislation fixing it` `an Act is to come into operation on a date to be fixed by subsidiary legislation` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `an Act is to come into operation on a date to be fixed by subsidiary legislation` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1156 | (ii) where the authority has been replaced wholly or
-- src:1157 | partially by another authority, the power conferred
-- src:1162 | herein upon the original authority may be exercised
-- src:1163 | by the replacing authority concerning all matters or
-- src:1164 | things within its jurisdiction as if it were the original
-- src:1165 | authority;
@ref s 19(a)(ii) (src:1156-1165)
GIVEN `the authority has been replaced wholly or partially by another authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the replacing authority may exercise the power over matters within its jurisdiction as if it were the original authority` `the authority has been replaced wholly or partially by another authority` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the authority has been replaced wholly or partially by another authority` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1167 | (b) when any Act confers powers on any authority to make
-- src:1168 | subsidiary legislation for any general purpose, and also for
-- src:1169 | any special purpose incidental thereto, the enumeration of
-- src:1170 | the special purposes does not derogate from the generality
-- src:1171 | of the powers conferred with reference to the general
-- src:1172 | purpose; and
@ref s 19(b) (src:1167-1172)
GIVEN `the power is conferred for a general purpose and also for a special purpose incidental to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the enumeration of the special purposes derogates from the generality of the power` `the power is conferred for a general purpose and also for a special purpose incidental to it` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the power is conferred for a general purpose and also for a special purpose incidental to it` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1174 | (c) subsidiary legislation made under an Act must not be
-- src:1175 | inconsistent with the provisions of any Act.
@ref s 19(c) (src:1174-1175)
GIVEN `the subsidiary legislation is inconsistent with a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsidiary legislation made under an Act is permitted` `the subsidiary legislation is inconsistent with a provision of an Act` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (NOT `the subsidiary legislation is inconsistent with a provision of an Act`)

§ `Section 20 -- additional provisions as to subsidiary legislation`

DECLARE `What authority to make subsidiary legislation includes` IS ONE OF
    `authority to provide that a contravention is punishable by a fine and imprisonment within the limits of section 20(a)(i)`
    `authority to amend forms prescribed by the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made`
    `authority to prescribe new forms`
    `authority to provide for submitting, issuing or serving a document, record, application, permit, approval or licence by electronic means, or for its authentication`
    `authority to provide for the manner and method of payment of fees and charges, and their reduction, waiver or refund`
    `authority to impose charges and penalties for late payment of fees and charges`
    `authority to impose interest on an outstanding fee, charge or penalty, or on payment by instalment`
    `something else`

-- src:1179 | 20. The following provisions also apply to subsidiary legislation:
-- src:1181 | (a) authority to make subsidiary legislation includes —
-- src:1183 | (i) authority to provide that a contravention thereof shall
-- src:1184 | be punishable by a fine not exceeding $2,000 or with
-- src:1185 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or
-- src:1186 | both as may be specified in the subsidiary legislation;
-- src:1188 | (ii) authority to amend any forms prescribed by the
-- src:1189 | written law under which the subsidiary legislation
-- src:1190 | was made;
-- src:1192 | (iii) authority to prescribe new forms for the purpose
-- src:1193 | thereof and for the purpose of the subsidiary
-- src:1194 | legislation; and
-- src:1196 | (iv) authority to provide for the manner and method in
-- src:1197 | which any document, record, application, permit,
-- src:1198 | approval or licence may be submitted, issued or
-- src:1199 | served by electronic means, or for the authentication
-- src:1200 | thereof;
-- src:1202 | (b) authority to provide for fees and charges shall include
-- src:1203 | authority to provide for —
-- src:1208 | (i) the determination of the manner and method of
-- src:1209 | payment and the reduction, waiver or refund thereof,
-- src:1210 | either generally or in any particular event or case or
-- src:1211 | class of cases or in the discretion of any person; and
-- src:1213 | (ii) the imposition of —
-- src:1215 | (A) charges and penalties for the late payment
-- src:1216 | thereof; and
-- src:1218 | (B) interest on any outstanding amount of any fee,
-- src:1219 | charge or penalty referred to in this paragraph
-- src:1220 | or for any payment thereof by instalment; and
-- src:1222 | [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]
@ref s 20(a), (b) (src:1179-1222)
GIVEN `the authority asked about` IS A `What authority to make subsidiary legislation includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `the authority asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the authority asked about`
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 20(a)(i): a fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or both.
@ref s 20(a)(i) the penalty limits (src:1183-1186)
GIVEN `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months` MEANS
    `the fine in dollars` AT MOST 2000 AND `the imprisonment in months` AT MOST 12

-- src:1224 | (c) a reference in a written law to another written law includes
-- src:1225 | a reference to any subsidiary legislation made thereunder.
@ref s 20(c) (src:1224-1225)
GIVEN `a written law refers to another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference includes any subsidiary legislation made under the other written law` `a written law refers to another written law` MEANS
    `a written law refers to another written law`

§ `Section 21 -- use of defined terms in subsidiary legislation`

-- src:1229 | 21. Where any Act confers powers to make any subsidiary
-- src:1230 | legislation, expressions used in the subsidiary legislation have the
-- src:1231 | same meanings as in the Act conferring the power, unless the contrary
-- src:1232 | intention appears.
@ref s 21 (src:1229-1232)
GIVEN `an Act confers power to make subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`expressions in the subsidiary legislation have the same meanings as in the Act conferring the power` `an Act confers power to make subsidiary legislation` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `an Act confers power to make subsidiary legislation` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 22 -- anticipatory exercise of powers`

DECLARE `What the anticipatory exercise is for` IS ONE OF
    `bringing the Act or part into operation`
    `giving full effect to the Act or part on or after the day it comes into operation`
    `something else`

-- src:1236 | 22. Where an Act or any part thereof does not come into operation
-- src:1237 | immediately on its passing and the Act or that part confers power (or
-- src:1238 | amends another Act to confer power) to make subsidiary legislation
-- src:1239 | or to make appointments or to issue notifications or to prescribe forms
-- src:1240 | or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Act or that part (or the
-- src:1241 | Act being amended), then, unless the contrary intention appears, the
-- src:1242 | power may be exercised and any subsidiary legislation, appointment,
-- src:1243 | form or thing made, issued, prescribed or done under the power may
-- src:1244 | be made, issued, prescribed or done so as to take effect at any time
-- src:1245 | after the passing of the Act so far as may be necessary or expedient
-- src:1246 | for the purpose of —
-- src:1248 | (a) bringing the Act or that part into operation; or
-- src:1253 | (b) giving full effect to the Act or that part (or the other Act as
-- src:1254 | amended) on or after the day on which it comes into
-- src:1255 | operation.
-- src:1257 | [4/2021]
@ref s 22 (src:1236-1257)
GIVEN `the Act or part does not come into operation immediately on its passing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or part confers a power of the kinds s 22 lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what it is for` IS A `What the anticipatory exercise is for`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` `the Act or part does not come into operation immediately on its passing` `the Act or part confers a power of the kinds s 22 lists` `what it is for` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the Act or part does not come into operation immediately on its passing`
       AND `the Act or part confers a power of the kinds s 22 lists`
       AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `what it is for`
         WHEN `bringing the Act or part into operation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `giving full effect to the Act or part on or after the day it comes into operation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 23 -- commencement of subsidiary legislation`

-- src:1261 | 23.—(1) Subsidiary legislation made under any Act or other lawful
-- src:1262 | authority —
-- src:1264 | (a) unless it is otherwise expressly provided in any Act, must
-- src:1265 | be published in the Gazette; and
@ref s 23(1)(a) (src:1261-1265)
GIVEN `an Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsidiary legislation must be published in the Gazette` `an Act otherwise expressly provides` MEANS
    NOT `an Act otherwise expressly provides`

-- Section 23(1)(b) fixes the day; section 10(1)(b) (in the time module) fixes the moment within it.
-- src:1267 | (b) unless it is otherwise provided in the subsidiary legislation,
-- src:1268 | takes effect and comes into operation on the date of its
-- src:1269 | publication.
@ref s 23(1)(b) (src:1267-1269)
GIVEN `the date of publication` IS A DATE
      `a date the subsidiary legislation itself provides` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day subsidiary legislation takes effect and comes into operation` `the date of publication` `a date the subsidiary legislation itself provides` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a date the subsidiary legislation itself provides`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of publication`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d

-- src:1271 | (2) Any such subsidiary legislation may be made to operate
-- src:1272 | retrospectively to any date not being a date earlier than the
-- src:1273 | commencement of the Act or the establishment of the authority by
-- src:1274 | or under which the subsidiary legislation is made.
@ref s 23(2) (src:1271-1274)
GIVEN `the date it is to operate from` IS A DATE
      `the commencement of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the establishment of the authority` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` `the date it is to operate from` `the commencement of the Act` `the establishment of the authority` MEANS
    `the date it is to operate from` AT LEAST `the commencement of the Act`
    AND CONSIDER `the establishment of the authority`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST e THEN `the date it is to operate from` AT LEAST e

§ `Sections 24 to 26A`

-- src:1278 | 24. Judicial notice is to be taken of all subsidiary legislation made
-- src:1279 | or purporting to be made under any Act or other lawful authority.
@ref s 24 (src:1278-1279)
GIVEN `it is made or purports to be made under an Act or other lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`judicial notice is to be taken of the subsidiary legislation` `it is made or purports to be made under an Act or other lawful authority` MEANS
    `it is made or purports to be made under an Act or other lawful authority`

-- src:1283 | 25. Where subsidiary legislation amends other subsidiary
-- src:1284 | legislation, the amending subsidiary legislation is, so far as is
-- src:1285 | consistent with the tenor thereof and unless the contrary intention
-- src:1286 | appears, to be construed as one with the amended subsidiary
-- src:1287 | legislation.
@ref s 25 (src:1283-1287)
GIVEN `subsidiary legislation amends other subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `construing it as one with the amended subsidiary legislation is consistent with its tenor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the amending subsidiary legislation is construed as one with the amended subsidiary legislation` `subsidiary legislation amends other subsidiary legislation` `construing it as one with the amended subsidiary legislation is consistent with its tenor` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `subsidiary legislation amends other subsidiary legislation` AND `construing it as one with the amended subsidiary legislation is consistent with its tenor` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1292 | 26. An act is deemed to be done under any Act or by virtue of the
-- src:1293 | powers conferred by any Act or in pursuance or execution of the
-- src:1294 | powers of, or under the authority of any Act, if it is done under, or by
-- src:1295 | virtue of, or in pursuance of, subsidiary legislation made under any
-- src:1296 | power contained in the Act.
@ref s 26 (src:1292-1296)
GIVEN `the act is done under, by virtue of or in pursuance of subsidiary legislation made under a power contained in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the act is deemed to be done under the Act` `the act is done under, by virtue of or in pursuance of subsidiary legislation made under a power contained in the Act` MEANS
    `the act is done under, by virtue of or in pursuance of subsidiary legislation made under a power contained in the Act`

-- src:1303 | 26A. Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any
-- src:1304 | written law to an Act is to be construed so as to include a reference to
-- src:1305 | any subsidiary legislation made under that Act.
@ref s 26A (src:1303-1305)
GIVEN `a written law refers to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under that Act` `a written law refers to an Act` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law refers to an Act` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
